// @check
// @error argument 1: operator '==' is not defined for string and i32
// AN UN-ANNOTATED SCRUTINEE DEFERS, IT DOES NOT GUESS (D1572). A hole cannot decide the arm
// compares here, so each integer-literal arm records the same deferred `==` constraint the
// hand-written `if id == 0x10` twin records, and the CALL that pins the parameter adjudicates
// it. Passing a `string` is therefore refused AT THE ARGUMENT, in the twin's exact words —
// which is the property that matters: `match` neither invents an `i32` annotation the author
// did not write nor loses the refusal the twin already gave.

function len(id) {
  match id {
    0x10 => 14
    _ => -1
  }
}

print(len("a"))
